    "# Solución analítica\n",
    "\n",
    "Supongamos una barra metálica de longitud $L$, cuyos extremos se mantienen a temperaturas constantes $T_a$ y $T_b$. Sea $T_0$ la temperatura inicial uniforme de la barra.\n",
    "\n",
    "Al cabo de un tiempo suficientemente largo se alcanza un estado estacionario en el cual la temperatura deja de depender del tiempo. En ese régimen, la ley de Fourier implica una distribución lineal:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "T_e(x)=T_a+\\frac{T_b-T_a}{L}x.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Para estudiar el régimen transitorio escribimos\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "T(x,t)=T_e(x)+u(x,t),\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "donde $u(x,t)$ representa la parte transitoria.\n",
    "\n",
    "La ecuación de difusión del calor es\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{\\partial T}{\\partial t}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\alpha\n",
    "\\frac{\\partial^2T}{\\partial x^2},\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "siendo\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\alpha=\\frac{K}{\\rho c}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "la difusividad térmica del material.\n",
    "\n",
    "Como $T_e(x)$ satisface la ecuación estacionaria,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{d^2T_e}{dx^2}=0,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "la función $u(x,t)$ verifica\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial t}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\alpha\n",
    "\\frac{\\partial^2u}{\\partial x^2},\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "con condiciones de contorno homogéneas\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "u(0,t)=0,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "u(L,t)=0.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Buscamos una solución por separación de variables de la forma\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "u(x,t)=F(x)G(t).\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Sustituyendo en la ecuación de difusión,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{1}{\\alpha G}\n",
    "\\frac{dG}{dt}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\frac{1}{F}\n",
    "\\frac{d^2F}{dx^2}\n",
    "=\n",
    "-\\lambda,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "donde $\\lambda>0$ es una constante de separación.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Dependencia temporal\n",
    "\n",
    "La ecuación para $G(t)$ es\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{dG}{dt}\n",
    "+\n",
    "\\alpha\\lambda G\n",
    "=\n",
    "0,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "cuya solución es\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "G(t)=G(0)e^{-\\alpha\\lambda t}.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "## Dependencia espacial\n",
    "\n",
    "La ecuación para $F(x)$ es\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{d^2F}{dx^2}\n",
    "+\n",
    "\\lambda F\n",
    "=\n",
    "0.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Su solución general es\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "F(x)=A\\cos(\\sqrt{\\lambda}\\,x)\n",
    "+\n",
    "B\\sin(\\sqrt{\\lambda}\\,x).\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "La condición\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "u(0,t)=0\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "implica\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "A=0,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "por lo que\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "F(x)=B\\sin(\\sqrt{\\lambda}\\,x).\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Imponiendo\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "u(L,t)=0,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "se obtiene\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\sin(\\sqrt{\\lambda}\\,L)=0,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "de donde\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\sqrt{\\lambda_n}=\\frac{n\\pi}{L},\n",
    "\\qquad n=1,2,3,\\ldots\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "y por tanto\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\lambda_n=\n",
    "\\frac{n^2\\pi^2}{L^2}.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "La solución transitoria es\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "u(x,t)\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\n",
    "a_n\n",
    "\\exp\\left(\n",
    "-\\alpha\\frac{n^2\\pi^2}{L^2}t\n",
    "\\right)\n",
    "\\sin\\left(\n",
    "\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}\n",
    "\\right).\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Finalmente,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "T(x,t)\n",
    "=\n",
    "T_a+\\frac{T_b-T_a}{L}x\n",
    "+\n",
    "\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\n",
    "a_n\n",
    "\\exp\\left(\n",
    "-\\alpha\\frac{n^2\\pi^2}{L^2}t\n",
    "\\right)\n",
    "\\sin\\left(\n",
    "\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}\n",
    "\\right).\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "## Determinación de los coeficientes\n",
    "\n",
    "La condición inicial es\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "T(x,0)=T_0.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Entonces\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "T_0\n",
    "=\n",
    "T_a+\\frac{T_b-T_a}{L}x\n",
    "+\n",
    "\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\n",
    "a_n\n",
    "\\sin\\left(\n",
    "\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}\n",
    "\\right),\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "o equivalentemente,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "T_0-T_a-\\frac{T_b-T_a}{L}x\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\n",
    "a_n\n",
    "\\sin\\left(\n",
    "\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}\n",
    "\\right).\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Los coeficientes se obtienen mediante la serie de Fourier seno:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "a_n=\n",
    "\\frac{2}{L}\n",
    "\\int_0^L\n",
    "\\left(\n",
    "T_0-T_a-\\frac{T_b-T_a}{L}x\n",
    "\\right)\n",
    "\\sin\\left(\n",
    "\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}\n",
    "\\right)\\,dx.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Para una temperatura inicial uniforme $T_0$, se obtiene\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "a_n=\n",
    "\\frac{2}{n\\pi}\n",
    "\\left[\n",
    "(T_0-T_a)\n",
    "-\n",
    "(-1)^n(T_0-T_b)\n",
    "\\right].\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Equivalentemente,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "a_n=\n",
    "\\begin{cases}\n",
    "\\dfrac{2}{n\\pi}(2T_0-T_a-T_b),\n",
    "& n \\text{ impar},\n",
    "\\\\[0.4cm]\n",
    "\\dfrac{2}{n\\pi}(T_b-T_a),\n",
    "& n \\text{ par}.\n",
    "\\end{cases}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Por tanto, la solución completa queda dada por\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "T(x,t)\n",
    "=\n",
    "T_a+\\frac{T_b-T_a}{L}x\n",
    "+\n",
    "\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\n",
    "a_n\n",
    "\\exp\\left(\n",
    "-\\alpha\\frac{n^2\\pi^2}{L^2}t\n",
    "\\right)\n",
    "\\sin\\left(\n",
    "\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}\n",
    "\\right).\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\alpha=\\frac{K}{\\rho c}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "## Referencia\n",
    "[1] Matías Ortiz Díez, *Beginner's Introduction to Numerical Simulation in Python I: Solving the Heat Equation*, Medium.\n",
    "\n",
    "https://medium.com/@matiasortizdiez/beginners-introduction-to-natural-simulation-in-python-i-solving-the-heat-equation-bf0ae5d4c37f\n",
    "\n",
    "[2] Ángel Franco García, *La conducción del calor. Ley de Fourier*. Universidad del País Vasco (UPV/EHU).\n",
    "\n",
    "http://www.sc.ehu.es/sbweb/fisica_/transporte/cond_calor/conduccion/conduccion.html\n",
    "\n"
   ]
