    "# Extensión al caso tridimensional\n",
    "\n",
    "Consideremos ahora un sólido tridimensional de dimensiones $L_x$, $L_y$ y $L_z$, cuya temperatura depende de la posición y del tiempo,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "T=T(x,y,z,t).\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "La ecuación de difusión del calor en tres dimensiones viene dada por\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{\\partial T}{\\partial t}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\alpha\n",
    "\\left(\n",
    "\\frac{\\partial^2T}{\\partial x^2}\n",
    "+\n",
    "\\frac{\\partial^2T}{\\partial y^2}\n",
    "+\n",
    "\\frac{\\partial^2T}{\\partial z^2}\n",
    "\\right),\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "donde\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\alpha=\\frac{K}{\\rho c}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "es la difusividad térmica del material.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Separación de variables\n",
    "\n",
    "Buscamos una solución de la forma\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "T(x,y,z,t)=X(x)Y(y)Z(z)G(t).\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Sustituyendo en la ecuación de difusión obtenemos\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{1}{\\alpha G}\n",
    "\\frac{dG}{dt}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\frac{1}{X}\n",
    "\\frac{d^2X}{dx^2}\n",
    "+\n",
    "\\frac{1}{Y}\n",
    "\\frac{d^2Y}{dy^2}\n",
    "+\n",
    "\\frac{1}{Z}\n",
    "\\frac{d^2Z}{dz^2}.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Como el miembro izquierdo depende únicamente del tiempo y el derecho únicamente de las coordenadas espaciales, ambos deben ser iguales a una constante negativa. Introduciendo las constantes de separación,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\lambda_x,\\qquad\n",
    "\\lambda_y,\\qquad\n",
    "\\lambda_z,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "se obtiene\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{1}{X}\n",
    "\\frac{d^2X}{dx^2}\n",
    "=-\\lambda_x,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{1}{Y}\n",
    "\\frac{d^2Y}{dy^2}\n",
    "=-\\lambda_y,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{1}{Z}\n",
    "\\frac{d^2Z}{dz^2}\n",
    "=-\\lambda_z,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "y\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{1}{\\alpha G}\n",
    "\\frac{dG}{dt}\n",
    "=\n",
    "-(\\lambda_x+\\lambda_y+\\lambda_z).\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "## Dependencia temporal\n",
    "\n",
    "La ecuación para la parte temporal es\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{dG}{dt}\n",
    "+\n",
    "\\alpha\n",
    "(\\lambda_x+\\lambda_y+\\lambda_z)\n",
    "G\n",
    "=\n",
    "0,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "cuya solución es\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "G(t)\n",
    "=\n",
    "G(0)\n",
    "\\exp\n",
    "\\left[\n",
    "-\\alpha\n",
    "(\\lambda_x+\\lambda_y+\\lambda_z)t\n",
    "\\right].\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "## Dependencia espacial\n",
    "\n",
    "Las ecuaciones para las componentes espaciales son\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{d^2X}{dx^2}\n",
    "+\n",
    "\\lambda_xX\n",
    "=\n",
    "0,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{d^2Y}{dy^2}\n",
    "+\n",
    "\\lambda_yY\n",
    "=\n",
    "0,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{d^2Z}{dz^2}\n",
    "+\n",
    "\\lambda_zZ\n",
    "=\n",
    "0.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Sus soluciones son funciones seno y coseno. Para condiciones de contorno homogéneas se obtienen las autofunciones\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "X_n(x)\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\sin\n",
    "\\left(\n",
    "\\frac{n\\pi x}{L_x}\n",
    "\\right),\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "Y_m(y)\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\sin\n",
    "\\left(\n",
    "\\frac{m\\pi y}{L_y}\n",
    "\\right),\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "Z_p(z)\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\sin\n",
    "\\left(\n",
    "\\frac{p\\pi z}{L_z}\n",
    "\\right),\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "donde\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "n,m,p=1,2,3,\\ldots\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "y los valores propios asociados son\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\lambda_x=\n",
    "\\left(\n",
    "\\frac{n\\pi}{L_x}\n",
    "\\right)^2,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\lambda_y=\n",
    "\\left(\n",
    "\\frac{m\\pi}{L_y}\n",
    "\\right)^2,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\lambda_z=\n",
    "\\left(\n",
    "\\frac{p\\pi}{L_z}\n",
    "\\right)^2.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "## Solución general\n",
    "\n",
    "Por tanto, la solución tridimensional puede expresarse como\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "T(x,y,z,t)\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\n",
    "\\sum_{m=1}^{\\infty}\n",
    "\\sum_{p=1}^{\\infty}\n",
    "a_{nmp}\n",
    "\\exp\n",
    "\\left[\n",
    "-\\alpha\\pi^2\n",
    "\\left(\n",
    "\\frac{n^2}{L_x^2}\n",
    "+\n",
    "\\frac{m^2}{L_y^2}\n",
    "+\n",
    "\\frac{p^2}{L_z^2}\n",
    "\\right)t\n",
    "\\right]\n",
    "\\sin\n",
    "\\left(\n",
    "\\frac{n\\pi x}{L_x}\n",
    "\\right)\n",
    "\\sin\n",
    "\\left(\n",
    "\\frac{m\\pi y}{L_y}\n",
    "\\right)\n",
    "\\sin\n",
    "\\left(\n",
    "\\frac{p\\pi z}{L_z}\n",
    "\\right),\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "donde los coeficientes $a_{nmp}$ se determinan a partir de la distribución inicial de temperaturas,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "T(x,y,z,0)=T_0(x,y,z),\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "mediante una serie triple de Fourier.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Estado estacionario\n",
    "\n",
    "A medida que transcurre el tiempo,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "t\\rightarrow\\infty,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "los términos exponenciales se atenúan y la solución converge hacia el estado estacionario, determinado por la ecuación de Laplace\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\nabla^2T=0,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "es decir,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{\\partial^2T}{\\partial x^2}\n",
    "+\n",
    "\\frac{\\partial^2T}{\\partial y^2}\n",
    "+\n",
    "\\frac{\\partial^2T}{\\partial z^2}\n",
    "=\n",
    "0.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "La rapidez con que se alcanza dicho equilibrio depende de la difusividad térmica\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\alpha=\\frac{K}{\\rho c},\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "de manera que materiales con mayor difusividad alcanzan más rápidamente una distribución uniforme de temperatura."
